titles.refresh_control:
A command-line switch, -freq <hz>. CONFIRMED.

String evidence (strings -a -t x): '-freq' at file offset 0x18cb0c, in the video-mode block beside -width/-height/-forceres/-window/-full, and at 0x17e434, in the D3D wrapper.

The OpenGL method: vtable 0x1e4a5f0 has COL 0x1e555b0, whose TypeDescriptor is .?AVCVideoMode_OpenGL@@. Slot 17 (0x1e4a634) is 0x1dc75f0, which:
- returns if windowed;
- builds a DEVMODE with dmSize 0x94, w/h/bpp from the current mode, and dmFields 0x1C0000;
- if COM_CheckParm("-freq") matches (a byte-exact, case-sensitive compare at 0x1d367d0), sets dmDisplayFrequency = atoi(argv[i+1]) and ORs dmFields with 0x400000;
- calls ChangeDisplaySettingsA(&dm, 4) at 0x1dc7684 and discards the result.

The only other CDS call is the (NULL,0) restore at 0x1dc75cd. There is no refresh cvar (only r_norefresh, timerefresh, r_glowshellfreq), no -refresh switch and no registry value.

Evidence status: the GL-path -freq in build 4554 is proven by disassembly only. The hardware precedent (FINDINGS 2026-08-03: '-freq 100 honored... without it 60 Hz') was the Bcs16 build in D3D mode.

On .124 the ICD and Glide decide instead: fxBestRefresh, then the h5 Glide's IDirectDraw2::SetDisplayMode with the requested rate, with FX_GLIDE_REFRESH as an override.
